# Games

`games` is the terminal-game launcher from
[`keys-i/tools`](https://github.com/keys-i/tools). The `action` may be `list`,
`info`, or `run`. Choose a `game` for details or launch; choose a `format` of
`--plain` or `--json` when listing.

Interactive games cannot run inside the dashboard output pane. Selecting
`run` shows the exact direct-terminal command. The launcher resolves one
installed executable and starts it without a shell. Missing games produce the
upstream source URL instead of downloading anything.

Additional game packs are bounded `*.game` manifests loaded by the Rust tool
from `TOOLS_GAME_PATH` or the user data directory. This scripts pack contains
only the shared manual and typed UI contract; it does not duplicate launcher
logic. The prepared `keys-tools` PyPI package has not been published.
